[32m+[m[32m## Run it[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Option A — Docker Compose (recommended)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mcp .env.example .env          # adjust SECRET_KEY in production[m
[32m+[m[32mdocker compose up --build[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Frontend + API: `http://localhost` (Nginx routes `/api/*` to the backend)[m
[32m+[m[32m- API docs: `http://localhost/api/v1/openapi.json`[m
[32m+[m[32m- FastAPI docs (direct): `http://localhost:8000/docs`[m
[32m+[m[32m- PostgreSQL on `5432`, Redis on `6379`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMigrations run automatically on backend container start (`alembic upgrade head`).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe instrument catalog is reference data only and is never fetched from a[m
[32m+[m[32mbroker. Seed it once (or re-run to update non-destructively):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mcd backend[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m app.seed                 # all exchanges[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m app.seed --exchange NSE  # single exchange[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Option B — Local development[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32m# 1. Start infrastructure[m
[32m+[m[32mdocker compose up db redis[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# 2. Backend (http://localhost:8000)[m
[32m+[m[32mcd backend[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate[m
[32m+[m[32mpip install -e ".[dev]"[m
[32m+[m[32malembic upgrade head[m
[32m+[m[32muvicorn app.main:app --reload[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# 3. Frontend (http://localhost:3000)[m
[32m+[m[32mcd frontend[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm install[m
[32m+[m[32mNEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000 npm run dev[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe frontend proxies `/api/*` to the backend so you can always use[m
[32m+[m[32m`http://localhost:3000/api/v1/...`.[m
[32m+[m
