[32m+[m[32m## Security notes[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Access tokens are returned in the response body and must be kept in memory by the SPA[m
[32m+[m[32m  (they are not stored in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Refresh tokens are set as `httpOnly` cookies; `Secure` is enabled when[m
[32m+[m[32m  `ENVIRONMENT=production`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `SECRET_KEY` is validated at startup: production refuses the placeholder value[m
[32m+[m[32m  and any key shorter than 32 characters.[m
[32m+[m[32m- CSRF: the API is bearer-token based (no cookie-authenticated state-changing[m
[32m+[m[32m  requests), so CSRF protection applies once cookie-based flows are introduced.[m
[32m+[m[32m- No broker credentials are stored or handled anywhere yet.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Portfolio ownership is enforced server-side (never trusted from the request[m
[32m+[m[32m  body); a user cannot read or mutate another tenant's portfolios.[m
[32m+[m[32m- All market data is simulated and explicitly labelled (`is_mock: true`); the[m
[32m+[m[32m  provider abstraction ensures real feeds cannot be mistaken for mock data.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Known limitations / deferred to later phases[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Docker cannot be exercised in the current sandbox; the compose file and[m
[32m+[m[32m  Dockerfiles are authored and YAML-validated but not yet built here.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Local verification used SQLite; the CI pipeline runs the full Postgres + Redis[m
[32m+[m[32m  migration and test path.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Auth session is in-memory on the frontend: a page reload loses the access[m
[32m+[m[32m  token (refresh-cookie flow is implemented server-side and will be wired up).[m
[32m+[m[32m- No email verification, MFA/2FA, password reset yet (skeleton only).[m
[32m+[m[32m- The instrument catalog is static reference data seeded into the DB; real[m
[32m+[m[32m  instrument-master synchronisation from a broker/exchange feed is deferred.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Market quotes are synthetic (`MockMarketDataProvider`); no real tick data or[m
[32m+[m[32m  WebSocket streaming yet. Quotes are cached 2s in Redis.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Orders, positions, P&L, strategies, backtesting, broker adapters, news, AI[m
[32m+[m[32m  and notifications are the subject of later phases.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Rate limiting falls back to in-memory when Redis is unreachable (single-node[m
[32m+[m[32m  only; not for multi-instance deployments).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Manual testing checklist (Phase 1)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Register a new account → lands on dashboard, shows account details.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Dashboard → **Portfolios**: create one (name + capital), it appears in the list.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Create a second portfolio with the same name → friendly 409 error shown.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. Dashboard → **Market quotes**: default `RELIANCE,TCS,NIFTY` loads mock quotes[m
[32m+[m[32m   (each row tagged `mock`); change symbols and refresh.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. Request an unknown symbol (e.g. `ZZZZ`) → friendly 404 error shown.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. Delete a portfolio → it disappears from the list.[m
[32m+[m[32m7. Sign out → returns to login; login again → portfolios still listed.[m
[32m+[m[32m8. Direct hit on `/api/v1/portfolios` or `/api/v1/market/quotes` without a token → 401.[m
[32m+[m[32m9. With Docker: `docker compose up --build` then repeat the above via `http://localhost`.[m
[32m+[m[32m10. Confirm `/docs` renders the OpenAPI schema for the new endpoints.[m
